    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nPressing `Ctrl-Z` (or triggering `:suspend`) inside Neovim while it is invoked via a non-interactive shell layout completely traps the host terminal configuration in an unresponsive raw-mode freeze. \n\nUnlike interactive shell processes, non-interactive shell wrappers lack a running job-control engine context to restore cooked attributes or return a viable terminal prompt. Neovim blindly triggers its internal `SIGTSTP` handover directly to the kernel anyway. This results in the editor locking up instantly while keeping the input matrix bound to an unmanaged background thread.\n\n**Contrast to other TUIs:** Other system text interfaces such as `htop` proactively query process group capability or safeguard active signals to avoid self-orphaning under unmanaged wrappers. Neovim drops all responsiveness by default.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI reproduced this by opening the \".desktop\" launcher gnome or XFCE then using ctrl-z.  \n\nTested this with gnome and xfce on Linux though I am sure this is DE agnostic and assume that the issue even occurs on other OSs such MacOS or Windows when running on non-interactive shell.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNeovim immediately halts execution threads. The terminal console retains raw window attributes, rendering all standard typing completely inert and the neovim session can no longer be recovered.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNeovim should implement defensive runtime checks prior to committing to a total `SIGTSTP` suspension loop. If it evaluates that it is executing without an active interactive process coordinator (e.g. evaluating if job control options are completely absent in the host shell process), it should safely reject the operation with a warning or fallback action, preventing an unrecoverable terminal freeze.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n`NVIM v0.12.4`\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nSorry no vim on my system\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 7.1.8-1-cachyos\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nxfce4-terminal v1.2.0 (but also tested on alacritty and gnome-terminal)\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\n`xterm-256color`\n\n### Installation\n\n`pacman -S nvim`",
